From 229cf0621950919c38a271ab3c07dfd41dd301d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aloka Dixit <aloka.dixit@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:10:57 -0700
Subject: wifi: mac80211: remove redundant null check in ieee80211_assign_beacon()
Git-commit: 229cf0621950919c38a271ab3c07dfd41dd301d0
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: stable-fixes

The else-if branch condition 'old && old->mbssid_ies' already
guarantees 'old' is non-NULL. The inner 'old &&' in
'if (old && old->rnr_ies)' is therefore redundant; remove it.

Signed-off-by: Aloka Dixit <aloka.dixit@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261002-csa_cca_fix-v1-2-b83a998aeb44@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/mac80211/cfg.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/cfg.c b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
index 4eab9ab49d20..917594ad6474 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/cfg.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
@@ -1547,7 +1547,7 @@ ieee80211_assign_beacon(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 	} else if (old && old->mbssid_ies) {
 		mbssid = old->mbssid_ies;
 		size += struct_size(new->mbssid_ies, elem, mbssid->cnt);
-		if (old && old->rnr_ies) {
+		if (old->rnr_ies) {
 			rnr = old->rnr_ies;
 			size += struct_size(new->rnr_ies, elem, rnr->cnt);
 		}
-- 
